--- !u!114 &1908288687
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1908288686}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2e90d6c95be70497a88ccd6ddf88005b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LandNav.FeatureRegistry
  features:
  - id: knoll
    displayName: Knoll
    position: {x: 160, y: 49.147198, z: 335}
    radius: 18
    flag: 1
    teaching: 'A knoll is a rounded hilltop: ground falls away in every direction.
      On the map it is a small closed contour ring.'
  - id: ridge
    displayName: Ridgeline
    position: {x: 218.6534, y: 42.551918, z: 332.4941}
    radius: 16
    flag: 2
    teaching: A ridgeline is a line of high ground. Ground falls away on both sides
      but stays level or rises along it. Contours form long U or V shapes pointing
      away from high ground.
  - id: saddle
    displayName: Saddle
    position: {x: 277.15338, y: 31.137932, z: 327.9941}
    radius: 16
    flag: 3
    teaching: A saddle is the dip on a ridge between two high points. Ground rises
      in two directions (to each knoll) and falls in the other two. Contours look
      like an hourglass.
  - id: valley
    displayName: Valley
    position: {x: 262, y: 6.057575, z: 185}
    radius: 20
    flag: 4
    teaching: A valley is low ground between two spurs or ridges, usually with a
      watercourse. Contours form U or V shapes pointing uphill, towards higher ground.
  - id: knoll_east
    displayName: Knoll (the eastern one)
    position: {x: 355, y: 49.409615, z: 322}
    radius: 18
    flag: 0
    teaching: This is the other knoll on the map. Check which closed contour ring
      your flag is marked on.
